# Movies API (week 7) requests - validation, logging and JWT auth on the week 6 API.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then click
# "Send Request" above any request. Run them TOP TO BOTTOM: the login requests name
# their responses (bob, alice, carol) and later requests reuse those tokens.
# Prefer Postman? Import mflix-api.postman_collection.json instead.
#
# Start the server first:
#   docker compose exec node node week07/class2/mflix-api/server.js
# Watch that terminal as you go - every request is logged by morgan -> winston, and
# logins, rejections and changes get their own lines. Then open logs/combined.log.
#
#   alice / password123  admin   read, create, update, delete
#   bob   / letmein      editor  read, create, update
#   carol / hunter2      viewer  read only

@api = http://localhost:3001/api
@matrix = 573a139bf29313caabcf3d23

### ================= 1. READING IS STILL PUBLIC (no token) =================

### Search by title
GET {{api}}/movies?title=matrix

### Filter + pagination
GET {{api}}/movies?genre=Western&page=3&limit=5

### One movie
GET {{api}}/movies/{{matrix}}

### ================= 2. VALIDATION MIDDLEWARE (validate.js) =================

### 400 from validateId - the database is never asked
GET {{api}}/movies/banana

### 400 from validateMovieQuery - each problem listed
GET {{api}}/movies?year=nineteen&limit=5000&colour=blue

### 400 - ?title=a&title=b arrives as an ARRAY, not a string
GET {{api}}/movies?title=a&title=b

### ================= 3. WRITING WITHOUT A TOKEN =================

### 401 - requireJwt stops it before validation even runs
POST {{api}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "No token, no movie" }

### ================= 4. LOG IN =================

### 400 - validateLogin: nothing sent
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 401 - wrong password (same message as a wrong username - look at the terminal: logged as a warn)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "guess" }

### 401 - user that doesn't exist: same message, same speed
### ({{$guid}} = a new random username each time, so re-running this never trips the rate limit)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "mallory-{{$guid}}", "password": "letmein" }

### 200 - bob (editor). Paste the token into https://jwt.io: sub, role, iat, exp - no password
# @name bob
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "letmein" }

### 200 - alice (admin)
# @name alice
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "alice", "password": "password123" }

### 200 - carol (viewer)
# @name carol
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "carol", "password": "hunter2" }

### Who does bob's token say he is?
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}

### ================= 5. CRUD WITH A TOKEN =================

### 403 - carol is logged in (not 401) but a viewer can't create
POST {{api}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Carol's Movie" }

### 400 - bob may create, but validateMovie lists every problem
POST {{api}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "year": 1066, "runtime": "long", "genres": "Drama", "isAdmin": true, "$where": "1" }

### 201 - bob creates a movie. The terminal shows "Movie created ... by: bob"
# @name created
POST {{api}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "INET2005: Middleware Strikes Back",
  "year": 2026,
  "runtime": 95,
  "genres": ["Documentary", "Comedy"],
  "rated": "PG",
  "plot": "Students secure an API in an afternoon.",
  "directors": ["A. Student"]
}

### Read it back (public)
GET {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### 400 - PATCH with an empty body
PATCH {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 200 - PATCH: change only these fields
PATCH {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rated": "PG-13", "runtime": 102 }

### 200 - PUT: replace the whole movie
PUT {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "INET2005: The Director's Cut", "year": 2027 }

### 403 - bob is an editor; only admins delete
DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}

### 204 - alice is an admin
DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.token}}

### 404 - gone
GET {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### ================= 6. BAD TOKENS (all 401) =================

### Expired: alice's admin token from November 2023 (signed with the dev secret)
DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{matrix}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhbGljZSIsInJvbGUiOiJhZG1pbiIsImlhdCI6MTcwMDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMDAzNjAwfQ.9fvfqOmGJpr6Djd7Xy0JSxBRd2ubjgipQ9BMU_byyyY

### Forged: carol gave herself "role": "admin" and signed it with a secret she guessed
DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{matrix}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJjYXJvbCIsInJvbGUiOiJhZG1pbiIsImlhdCI6MTc5MDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxODkzNDU2MDAwfQ.0bjVhdEJ3bEIi9cnnWL27qOfBs4VYU40XpfNrUmsVjA

### "alg": "none" - no signature at all. Rejected because we only accept HS256
DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{matrix}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJjYXJvbCIsInJvbGUiOiJhZG1pbiJ9.

### Wrong scheme: "Token" instead of "Bearer"
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Token {{bob.response.body.token}}

### ================= 7. RATE LIMITING THE LOGIN (middleware/rateLimit.js) =================

### Click Send on this one SIX times. Tries 1-5: 401, and the RateLimit header counts down.
### Try 6: 429 Too Many Requests - and it stays 429 for 15 minutes, even with the right password.
### (eve isn't a real user, so this never locks out bob or alice. Restart the server to reset it.)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "eve", "password": "guess" }

### ================= 8. LOG OUT (the token really dies) =================

### A fresh login for bob, so logging out doesn't break the requests above
# @name bobAgain
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "letmein" }

### 200 - the token works
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bobAgain.response.body.token}}

### 204 - log out: the token's id (jti) goes in the revoked_tokens collection
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{bobAgain.response.body.token}}

### 401 - same token, still signed and not expired, but logged out
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bobAgain.response.body.token}}

### ================= 9. HELMET'S HEADERS =================

### Look at the response HEADERS, not the body: Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options,
### X-Frame-Options, Strict-Transport-Security... and no X-Powered-By
GET {{api}}/movies?limit=1

### ================= 10. THE ERROR HANDLER'S SAFETY NET =================

### 400 - body isn't valid JSON (express.json() throws, the error handler answers)
POST {{api}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ title: oops }

### 404 - no such API route (logged as a warn)
GET {{api}}/nope
